\name{cellucid_view_embedding_set}
\alias{cellucid_view_embedding_set}
\title{Show an embedding}
\usage{
cellucid_view_embedding_set(viewer, view, embedding)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{view}{A view: "View N" as the Compare views list numbers its rows (the live view is View 1 while it is shown, the kept views follow in the order they were kept). Text. Required.}
\item{embedding}{An embedding: the obsm array and the columns of it plotted. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{columns}}{The 0-based columns plotted, one per dimension. A vector or list of a whole number (at least 0) (at least 1 item, at most 3 items, each once). Required.}\item{\code{key}}{The obsm key, "X_umap". Text (at least 1 character). Required.}}}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Show one enabled embedding in a view; the view keeps it when the data mapping changes its defaults.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{view.embedding.set} (Views). It changes what the viewer shows: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{views}, \code{camera}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_view_embedding_set(viewer, embedding = list(columns = c(0,
      1), key = "X_umap"), view = "View 1")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
